From 61b185ccbdd0ddf0f76eed161c4e8802db5673cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:02:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sinker): compensate a Sinker Side Burn for electrode
 wear in Z

A Sinker Side Burn now takes a measured electrode wear and a layer
step. The plunge is burn_compensated's layered, wear-deepened plunge
under all of its refusals; the lateral move and its return run at the
last compensated tip, checked against the deepest-tip bound. The stock
sim reads the side burn as the worn electrode burns it. The by-name
refusals of a wear rate and a layer step on a side burn are removed; a
half-stated wear or a bad layer step is still refused by name.

Only the measured wear applies: the condition's wear rate is not applied
to a side burn, so saved side burns post byte for byte. Side wear is not
compensated (docs/decisions/1340-side-burn-wear.md). The side burn page
shows the layer and measured wear rows.

Fixes #1340
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
